      "message": "Chromium for Android complains that this is a global with a `CAPITALIZED_NAME` (or a `kCamelCaseName`) but it is in `.data` and not `.rodata`. This is because `SkMatrix` has a mutable field `fTypeMask`. While this object\u0027s `fTypeMask` isn\u0027t going to change, nothing prevents it being changed (it wouldn\u0027t be UB to change it) so it can\u0027t go in `.rodata`. The default constructor for `SkMatrix` is `constexpr` so this object should be constructed in `.data` at compile time, but it won\u0027t be write-protected.\n\nThis can be alleviated by naming it something else, like `identity`. Though it would be nice if SkMatrix didn\u0027t have hidden mutability.\n\nEasy enough to fix forward with a rename, however there is a desire to cherry-pick this change into Chromium 122. The best course for now is to revert and re-land.",
